---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Terminal, Cpu, Zap, Server, Database, Mail } from '@lucide/astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Me | Yashasav"
  description="Software engineer obsessed with cutting-edge LLM inference, kernel-level GPU optimizations, and building high-throughput distributed systems at scale."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-10">

    <!-- Hero Title -->
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 text-xs font-mono border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
        <Terminal class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-neutral-500" />
        <span>LLM Inference · GPU Optimizations · High-Throughput Systems</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
        About & Technical Journey
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Software engineer working at the intersection of <strong>cutting-edge LLM inference</strong>, GPU kernel-level optimizations, and high-throughput distributed systems. I go deep on how modern systems squeeze every last FLOP out of hardware—from CUDA memory hierarchies to event streaming internals and storage engines.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800" />

    <!-- Narrative Section -->
    <section class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
          Inference, Optimizations & GPU Systems
        </h2>
        <p>
          My deepest technical interest is in <strong>how inference systems actually work at the hardware level</strong>—not just the math of transformers, but why a naive attention implementation saturates HBM bandwidth, how tiling SRAM blocks eliminates intermediate reads/writes, and what it takes to serve thousands of concurrent requests efficiently.
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Attention Kernel Mechanics:</strong> Breaking down FlashAttention's IO-aware block tiling, Online Softmax rescaling, and how it achieves 3× speedups by keeping intermediate activations in SRAM—never touching HBM for S and P matrices.</li>
          <li><strong>KV Cache Memory Management:</strong> Deep analysis of PagedAttention (vLLM)—OS-style virtual paging for KV blocks—vs RadixAttention (SGLang)—prefix-tree based radix triage—and how each eliminates fragmentation to maximize GPU memory utilization across batches.</li>
          <li><strong>Serving Optimizations:</strong> Continuous batching, speculative decoding, chunked prefill, prefill-decode disaggregation, and KV cache quantization—the full stack of techniques that make production inference engines competitive.</li>
          <li><strong>GPU Architecture:</strong> Understanding compute- vs memory-bound operations, roofline models, warp-level parallelism, and what it means to actually saturate an H100's 3.35 TB/s HBM bandwidth versus its 33 TB/s SRAM.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
          High-Throughput Distributed Systems
        </h2>
        <p>
          In production, I build systems where throughput and latency aren't academic—they translate directly to business outcomes. My work centers on event-driven, low-latency architectures that handle millions of events per second:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Event Streaming Internals:</strong> Log-structured storage, partition strategies, segment indexing, zero-copy I/O, page cache patterns, consumer lag management, and backpressure under high write amplification.</li>
          <li><strong>High-Throughput Pipelines:</strong> Architecting resilient, low-latency state machines for inventory transitions and fulfillment operations at quick-commerce scale.</li>
          <li><strong>Databases & Storage:</strong> ACID storage engines, relational database internals, write-ahead logs, high-speed caching layers, and embedded LSM-tree storage.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">
          How I Think & Write
        </h2>
        <p>
          I write the kind of breakdowns I wish existed when I was first trying to understand these systems—<strong>first-principles, hardware-grounded, visual where possible</strong>. The blog is a mix of deep technical dives and mental models: not documentation, but the intuition behind why systems are built the way they are.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every post starts with a question I genuinely couldn't find a satisfying answer to: Why does standard attention run out of memory at large sequence lengths? What exactly does "zero-copy" mean and at what layer does it apply? How does a prefix tree actually eliminate redundant computation?
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Stack Cards Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-md border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900/60 bg-blue-50/50 dark:bg-blue-950/20 space-y-1.5">
        <Cpu class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400" />
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold">Core Interest</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Inference & GPU Kernels</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-mono">
          FlashAttention, PagedAttention, RadixAttention, vLLM, SGLang, CUDA, Speculative Decoding, KV Compression.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-card-light dark:bg-card-dark space-y-1.5">
        <Zap class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-500" />
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-500 font-bold">Production Work</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Distributed Streaming</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-mono">
          Event Streaming, Log-Structured Storage, Zero-Copy I/O, Consumer Lag, Backpressure, High-Throughput Pipelines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-4 rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-card-light dark:bg-card-dark space-y-1.5">
        <Database class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300" />
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-500 font-bold">Production Work</div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Databases & Platform</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-mono">
          Storage Engines, ACID Guarantees, Write-Ahead Logs, Caching Layers, Microservices, Platform Infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Contact & Connect Card -->
    <section class="p-5 rounded-md border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-100/50 dark:bg-neutral-900/50 space-y-3">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Connect & Collaborate</h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        Always open to discussing inference engine internals, GPU optimization techniques, high-throughput system design, or anything at the boundary of systems software and ML infrastructure.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Yashasv-Prajapati"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-md bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-neutral-100 text-white dark:text-neutral-900 text-xs font-medium hover:bg-neutral-800 dark:hover:bg-neutral-200 transition-colors"
        >
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 fill-current" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M12 0C5.37 0 0 5.37 0 12c0 5.31 3.435 9.795 8.205 11.385.6.105.825-.255.825-.57 0-.285-.015-1.23-.015-2.235-3.015.555-3.795-.735-4.035-1.41-.135-.345-.72-1.41-1.23-1.695-.42-.225-1.02-.78-.015-.795.945-.015 1.62.87 1.845 1.23 1.08 1.815 2.805 1.305 3.495.99.105-.78.42-1.305.765-1.605-2.67-.3-5.46-1.335-5.46-5.925 0-1.305.465-2.385 1.23-3.225-.12-.3-.54-1.53.12-3.18 0 0 1.005-.315 3.3 1.23.96-.27 1.98-.405 3-.405s2.04.135 3 .405c2.295-1.56 3.3-1.23 3.3-1.23.66 1.65.24 2.88.12 3.18.765.84 1.23 1.905 1.23 3.225 0 4.605-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.925.435.375.81 1.095.81 2.22 0 1.605-.015 2.895-.015 3.3 0 .315.225.69.825.57A12.02 12.02 0 0024 12c0-6.63-5.37-12-12-12z"/>
          </svg>
          <span>GitHub</span>
        </a>
        <a
